-- title:
--   Coset graph modulo r-units versus class-set degeneracy datum
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with $a<0$, $b<0$ and with $\mathbb{H}\otimes\mathbb{Q}_w$ a division algebra exactly at the place $w$ containing the prime $q'\ge 5$; let $N\ne 0$, let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order (an order maximal among orders containing it), let $R$ be an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ of maximal orders with $[\Lambda_1:R]=N$) with $R\le\Lambda$, let $r$ be a prime with $r\ne q'$ and $r\nmid N$, and let $v$ be the height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in `primeHeckeSet R r`, i.e. $n$ is in the finite adèle box of $R$, $r\,n^{-1}$ is in that box, while $n^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}n$ are not. Assume `meetOrder R n` $=R\cap nRn^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$, is preserved by conjugation by $n$, and that the shift $x\mapsto x\cdot n$ on `ClassSet (Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer (meetOrder R n))` is an involution; both class sets are finite. Put $\Gamma=$ `ProjAwayUnits R v`, the group of units of $\mathbb{H}$ lying in the local box units of $R$ at every place $w\ne v$, modulo the kernel of its action on $\mathrm{Vert}(R,v)=(\mathbb{H}\otimes\mathbb{Q}_v)^{\times}/\mathrm{level}(R,v)$, where $\mathrm{level}(R,v)$ is generated by the local box units of $R$ at $v$ together with the scalar units. Then there are bijections $e_V$ from the orbit quotient $\Gamma\backslash\mathrm{Vert}(R,v)$ to `ClassSet (Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer R)` and $e_E$ from the orbit quotient of $\Gamma$ on the darts of the graph `graph R v` $n_v$ (vertices adjacent when distinct and of the form $g$, $g k n_v$ with $k$ in the level) to `ClassSet (Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer (meetOrder R n))` such that: for every idèle unit $x$ all of whose components away from $v$ are $1$, $e_V$ sends the orbit of the class of $x_v$ to the double coset class of $x$; for every such $x$ and every dart $d$ with origin $x_v$ and terminus $x_v n_v$, $e_E$ sends the orbit of $d$ to the double coset class of $x$ for the stabiliser of `meetOrder R n`; and $e_V$, $e_E$ identify the quotient degeneracy datum (origin, terminus, and the width of an orbit, the cardinality of the stabiliser in $\Gamma$ of a representative dart) with `classSetDegeneracyData R n` (the forgetful map to classes for $R$, the shift by $n$, and the class weight `classWeight` of `meetOrder R n`). No squarefreeness is assumed of $N$.
--
--   This is the adèlic dictionary, in the form used by Kurihara and Jordan–Livné, between the quotient of the Bruhat–Tits-type coset graph at the auxiliary prime $r$ by the $r$-unit group of an Eichler order and the degeneracy datum on the class sets of $R$ and of $R\cap nRn^{-1}$. It feeds the comparison of the Mumford-side and class-set-side data in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation, and is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_quot_equiv_classSet_shift_forget_of_mumfordSideFrame`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_quot_equiv_classSet_shift_forget_of_mumfordSideFrame).
